1
00:00:17,401 --> 00:00:19,871
(Kang Hoon, Cho Hyun Chul, Kim Jeong Jin)

2
00:00:23,101 --> 00:00:25,111
(Lee E Dam, Moon Hee, Yoon Ga I)

3
00:00:33,011 --> 00:00:34,551
(Jeon Bae Soo, Lee Seo Hwan, Oh Eui Sik)

4
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:56,840
(Happy Anding)

5
00:00:56,841 --> 00:00:58,510
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

6
00:00:58,511 --> 00:00:59,740
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

7
00:00:59,741 --> 00:01:00,940
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

8
00:01:00,941 --> 00:01:02,140
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

9
00:01:02,141 --> 00:01:03,341
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

10
00:01:22,501 --> 00:01:23,971
- Gosh!
- Gosh, you scared me!

11
00:01:25,101 --> 00:01:26,201
- Who is that?
- What's going on?

12
00:01:26,531 --> 00:01:27,601
Who's that?

13
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:29,171
What's going on?

14
00:01:31,511 --> 00:01:33,271
- Darn it.
- Hey, stop. Don't go.

15
00:01:33,371 --> 00:01:34,411
Who knows what she might do?

16
00:01:34,481 --> 00:01:36,281
- Hey.
- Hey.

17
00:01:43,121 --> 00:01:44,121
I'm...

18
00:01:45,451 --> 00:01:46,751
that crazy girl.

19
00:02:06,271 --> 00:02:07,281
I'm...

20
00:02:09,111 --> 00:02:10,581
your fan.

21
00:02:12,611 --> 00:02:13,611
So please,

22
00:02:16,721 --> 00:02:17,921
don't disband.

23
00:02:21,761 --> 00:02:22,991
You can't.

24
00:02:24,191 --> 00:02:25,191
You can't disband.

25
00:02:53,451 --> 00:02:54,621
Eun Young really made a mess.

26
00:03:09,541 --> 00:03:12,911
Well, look at us all together again.

27
00:03:13,011 --> 00:03:15,941
Keep this up, and we'll be best friends. Cheers.

28
00:03:16,011 --> 00:03:17,651
All right, let's toast. Cheers.

29
00:03:22,981 --> 00:03:24,151
Wait, but...

30
00:03:24,921 --> 00:03:26,891
when you say you're a fan,

31
00:03:27,461 --> 00:03:30,991
you mean you're a fan who actually likes us, right?

32
00:03:31,791 --> 00:03:34,201
How long have you liked us?

33
00:03:36,231 --> 00:03:39,601
For about a year.

34
00:03:40,301 --> 00:03:43,671
A year? That's pretty long. A year is quite a while, isn't it?

35
00:03:45,471 --> 00:03:46,511
By the way,

36
00:03:47,741 --> 00:03:51,511
the pigeon and the drinks... Why did you do that?

37
00:03:55,181 --> 00:03:57,421
Well, about the drinks,

38
00:03:58,391 --> 00:03:59,951
I really had no idea.

39
00:04:00,921 --> 00:04:03,521
And the pigeon,

40
00:04:04,591 --> 00:04:05,891
there was a misunderstanding.

41
00:04:07,961 --> 00:04:09,131
I'm...

42
00:04:09,561 --> 00:04:13,331
I'm really sorry about that.

43
00:04:15,001 --> 00:04:18,571
Well, sure. Things happen. Yes, I totally get it.

44
00:04:21,411 --> 00:04:26,581
Can I keep asking questions? Why do you like us?

45
00:04:28,021 --> 00:04:30,081
- Pardon?
- I mean, what made you...

46
00:04:30,551 --> 00:04:33,991
become a fan?

47
00:04:34,591 --> 00:04:37,021
Do you know any of our comedy sketches?

48
00:04:37,331 --> 00:04:39,861
- What's your favorite one?
- Hey, come on...

49
00:04:40,391 --> 00:04:44,401
Cut it out. Her face is about to burst.

50
00:04:45,131 --> 00:04:47,901
I'm sorry. It's just, this is a first for me.

51
00:04:47,971 --> 00:04:49,501
Having a fan and all.

52
00:04:50,441 --> 00:04:51,471
To start with,

53
00:04:52,311 --> 00:04:54,341
you put your whole body into it on stage.

54
00:04:55,811 --> 00:04:57,381
That's your biggest charm.

55
00:04:57,881 --> 00:04:59,881
And I love how dedicated you are to your makeup and costumes.

56
00:05:00,011 --> 00:05:02,681
Personally, the "Woman with a Twist" sketch.

57
00:05:02,881 --> 00:05:06,251
It's about a cafe part-timer, so I really resonated with it.

58
00:05:06,721 --> 00:05:08,961
It was as if it were about me.

59
00:05:09,791 --> 00:05:11,560
And of course, the sketch...

60
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:14,501
that best captures the true identity of Asura,

61
00:05:14,961 --> 00:05:17,671
"Look here, look here." I love that one too.

62
00:05:23,341 --> 00:05:24,341
Yes.

63
00:05:25,511 --> 00:05:28,141
That's why I like you guys.

64
00:05:28,641 --> 00:05:29,711
Gosh, wait...

65
00:05:30,651 --> 00:05:32,981
You know all our sketches.

66
00:05:33,051 --> 00:05:35,251
I'm actually getting kind of choked up here.

67
00:05:39,651 --> 00:05:40,891
I'm going to ask her.

68
00:05:42,361 --> 00:05:44,031
Ask her what I'm supposed to do.

69
00:05:45,461 --> 00:05:48,731
That person has been watching us all this time,

70
00:05:50,061 --> 00:05:51,571
so she might know.

71
00:05:59,171 --> 00:06:03,311
Could I ask a question this time?

72
00:06:04,111 --> 00:06:05,581
Sure, go ahead.

73
00:06:07,921 --> 00:06:10,721
Why are you disbanding?

74
00:06:14,421 --> 00:06:18,561
Whatever the reason is, isn't this wrong?

75
00:06:18,861 --> 00:06:20,391
You have fans like me.

76
00:06:20,461 --> 00:06:24,431
To suddenly disband like this without warning,

77
00:06:24,701 --> 00:06:25,971
that's just too much.

78
00:06:26,631 --> 00:06:29,271
I'll promote your channel,

79
00:06:29,471 --> 00:06:33,271
start a fan club, and work hard. No, I'll do a great job.

80
00:06:34,011 --> 00:06:35,241
So please,

81
00:06:35,911 --> 00:06:39,281
could you reconsider?

82
00:06:40,411 --> 00:06:41,421
Please?

83
00:06:43,051 --> 00:06:44,051
Please?

84
00:06:45,121 --> 00:06:47,821
- Well...
- No, we can't.

85
00:06:50,791 --> 00:06:52,031
We already decided,

86
00:06:53,331 --> 00:06:55,401
and we already announced it, so take it back? No way.

87
00:06:57,271 --> 00:06:58,431
We can't undo it.

88
00:06:59,331 --> 00:07:00,431
We won't.

89
00:07:02,441 --> 00:07:04,611
Don't cut me off like that.

90
00:07:04,971 --> 00:07:08,241
Could you please reconsider just one more time?

91
00:07:12,451 --> 00:07:14,021
Let's go. I'm tired.

92
00:07:14,721 --> 00:07:17,750
- You can't just leave like this.
- Eun Young!

93
00:07:17,751 --> 00:07:19,621
You can at least think about it once.

94
00:07:19,751 --> 00:07:22,590
- Let go of this.
- No, just once.

95
00:07:22,591 --> 00:07:23,591
- No.
- Hey.

96
00:07:23,661 --> 00:07:25,090
You're stretching my shirt.

97
00:07:25,091 --> 00:07:27,091
- Eun Young, take it easy.
- What's your problem?

98
00:07:27,191 --> 00:07:29,231
Please, just this once.

99
00:07:29,301 --> 00:07:31,530
- Shall we toast? Cheers.
- What's wrong with you?

100
00:07:31,531 --> 00:07:32,531
Okay.

101
00:07:32,532 --> 00:07:34,341
(Episode 3: Lunatic vs. Lunatic)

102
00:07:34,471 --> 00:07:35,571
It's fine.

103
00:07:38,841 --> 00:07:41,141
Man, we actually had a fan.

104
00:07:41,341 --> 00:07:43,211
She wasn't a crazy girl. She was a super fan.

105
00:07:43,611 --> 00:07:44,781
She's crazy too.

106
00:07:44,951 --> 00:07:45,951
Don't leave. Let go. What's wrong?

107
00:07:46,011 --> 00:07:47,181
- Let go. What's wrong?
- Easy there.

108
00:07:47,321 --> 00:07:48,621
And what was with the pigeon?

109
00:07:51,121 --> 00:07:52,551
What about it? It can happen.

110
00:07:53,091 --> 00:07:54,291
She said she thought we needed it.

111
00:07:55,091 --> 00:07:57,091
The fact that she connects with you means she's not normal.

112
00:07:57,161 --> 00:07:59,561
First off, if her favorite sketch is "Look here, look here"...

113
00:07:59,861 --> 00:08:01,331
then she's definitely not normal.

114
00:08:01,831 --> 00:08:04,171
Even I'm too embarrassed to show that sketch to anyone.

115
00:08:05,071 --> 00:08:06,370
Hey, you're embarrassed?

116
00:08:06,371 --> 00:08:09,140
Should parents really be ashamed of their own child?

117
00:08:09,141 --> 00:08:10,171
Nonsense.

118
00:08:10,241 --> 00:08:12,441
Is that why every time we performed that,

119
00:08:12,471 --> 00:08:14,181
you secretly wore a mask all by yourself?

120
00:08:14,941 --> 00:08:16,341
It was the concept, you idiot. The concept.

121
00:08:16,581 --> 00:08:19,481
- The concept, you idiot.
- Concept, my foot.

122
00:08:19,581 --> 00:08:20,581
What, you punk?

123
00:08:21,981 --> 00:08:24,991
Still, there was at least one person.

124
00:08:29,261 --> 00:08:30,991
Someone who told us not to quit.

125
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:43,271
Yes.

126
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:45,811
It wasn't a total waste of time.

127
00:08:50,011 --> 00:08:52,081
Let's wash up and sleep. I'm beat.

128
00:08:57,691 --> 00:09:01,590
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry. I tried to leave as fast as I could,

129
00:09:01,591 --> 00:09:03,561
but clueless Manager Kim...

130
00:09:05,461 --> 00:09:06,491
Na Yeon.

131
00:09:17,341 --> 00:09:18,541
Na Yeon, guess what? We have a fan.

132
00:09:21,711 --> 00:09:22,741
A fan?

133
00:09:27,981 --> 00:09:29,121
What kind of fan?

134
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:33,390
My goodness. She brought that pigeon...

135
00:09:33,391 --> 00:09:34,561
all because of us.

136
00:09:34,921 --> 00:09:37,890
Since she did it out of love as a fan,

137
00:09:37,891 --> 00:09:39,531
it's not like we can get mad at her.

138
00:09:39,591 --> 00:09:43,531
Seriously, is this how stars feel when they have a die-hard fan?

139
00:09:44,731 --> 00:09:45,971
Look at you, Kim Nam Il.

140
00:09:46,971 --> 00:09:48,041
Are you that happy?

141
00:09:48,301 --> 00:09:49,741
Yes, I am.

142
00:09:51,471 --> 00:09:53,211
It means there's at least one person...

143
00:09:53,241 --> 00:09:54,411
who will remember us.

144
00:09:57,281 --> 00:09:58,781
Is it completely decided, then?

145
00:10:00,011 --> 00:10:01,021
Disbanding?

146
00:10:02,181 --> 00:10:03,181
Yes.

147
00:10:04,551 --> 00:10:06,051
Is it because of me?

148
00:10:07,721 --> 00:10:09,421
Because of our fight the other day?

149
00:10:12,961 --> 00:10:15,801
No, we should've done this long ago.

150
00:10:16,831 --> 00:10:18,401
We were just being foolish, clinging on.

151
00:10:19,101 --> 00:10:20,471
And you were the only one suffering.

152
00:10:20,871 --> 00:10:23,771
- Nam Il, I...
- Na Yeon, I'm going to get a job.

153
00:10:26,071 --> 00:10:29,540
- A job?
- I think it's time for me...

154
00:10:29,541 --> 00:10:30,781
to look for real work.

155
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:34,621
Don't you think I'd be good at something like sales?

156
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:36,781
You know I have a way with words.

157
00:10:39,491 --> 00:10:40,591
Well,

158
00:10:41,261 --> 00:10:45,131
as long as you're happy, I'm happy.

159
00:10:46,061 --> 00:10:47,061
Right?

160
00:10:49,201 --> 00:10:50,701
Mother.

161
00:10:52,001 --> 00:10:53,001
Hello, Mother.

162
00:10:53,071 --> 00:10:54,240
- Nam Il, it's been a while.
- Mom.

163
00:10:54,241 --> 00:10:56,801
Why did you buy so much? Let me carry that for you.

164
00:10:57,201 --> 00:10:58,471
It's not heavy.

165
00:11:00,071 --> 00:11:02,011
- I'm fine.
- Okay.

166
00:11:04,751 --> 00:11:07,251
Nam Il was just saying he missed you, Mom.

167
00:11:07,581 --> 00:11:08,650
Come upstairs and hang out for a bit.

168
00:11:08,651 --> 00:11:11,321
Next time. We have a family gathering today.

169
00:11:11,991 --> 00:11:13,351
Your Aunt Dong Hee is coming over, remember?

170
00:11:14,051 --> 00:11:15,920
It's not like they're strangers.

171
00:11:15,921 --> 00:11:17,391
They've had dinner together before.

172
00:11:19,791 --> 00:11:21,531
Wait a second.

173
00:11:22,301 --> 00:11:23,831
Na Yeon, I'm sorry.

174
00:11:24,331 --> 00:11:26,201
I completely forgot I had something to do at the theater.

175
00:11:26,901 --> 00:11:27,901
Right now?

176
00:11:28,271 --> 00:11:30,571
Yes. I'm sorry. I think I should get going.

177
00:11:30,801 --> 00:11:31,941
I'm sorry, Mother.

178
00:11:32,511 --> 00:11:33,871
I'll get out of your way.

179
00:11:35,581 --> 00:11:36,811
Have a wonderful time.

180
00:11:40,751 --> 00:11:42,481
- Nam Il.
- See you.

181
00:11:52,191 --> 00:11:53,461
What's wrong with you lately, Mom?

182
00:11:54,131 --> 00:11:55,301
What about me?

183
00:11:55,361 --> 00:11:57,431
Why are you always so cold to Nam Il?

184
00:11:57,731 --> 00:11:59,171
You used to adore him.

185
00:11:59,931 --> 00:12:02,071
You said you liked how cheerful and affectionate he was.

186
00:12:02,171 --> 00:12:04,911
That was then, and this is now. That's exactly why I dislike him.

187
00:12:07,311 --> 00:12:08,440
What?

188
00:12:08,441 --> 00:12:11,281
He's 34 and cluelessly cheerful with no plan, which I hate.

189
00:12:11,811 --> 00:12:13,411
And even when I give him the cold shoulder,

190
00:12:14,011 --> 00:12:16,051
he just smiles and clings to me all sweet like that,

191
00:12:16,321 --> 00:12:17,381
which I hate even more.

192
00:12:19,091 --> 00:12:20,551
Are you really going to marry him?

193
00:12:23,061 --> 00:12:24,931
Yes, I am.

194
00:12:25,131 --> 00:12:26,491
If it's not him, I'm not marrying anyone.

195
00:12:27,091 --> 00:12:28,331
Unbelievable.

196
00:12:29,261 --> 00:12:30,561
I can't stand by and watch this anymore.

197
00:12:30,631 --> 00:12:33,101
- I really want you two to break up.
- Mom.

198
00:12:33,171 --> 00:12:34,841
He should at least have a real job.

199
00:12:35,441 --> 00:12:37,271
An unknown comedian? My goodness.

200
00:12:37,771 --> 00:12:40,741
- That's his job.
- He said he was quitting anyway.

201
00:12:40,911 --> 00:12:43,141
He's quitting comedy and getting a regular job.

202
00:12:45,211 --> 00:12:47,051
So please, stop being like this.

203
00:12:48,121 --> 00:12:49,451
Nam Il is trying his best too.

204
00:12:56,021 --> 00:12:57,221
Darn it...

205
00:12:57,461 --> 00:12:59,931
Well, looking at your test results,

206
00:13:00,661 --> 00:13:03,431
and considering how the pain flared up again out of nowhere...

207
00:13:04,601 --> 00:13:08,271
Has anything been troubling you or stressing you out lately?

208
00:13:08,801 --> 00:13:09,841
No.

209
00:13:11,671 --> 00:13:13,041
No, nothing like that at all.

210
00:13:13,941 --> 00:13:17,711
Emotional distress can manifest as physical pain.

211
00:13:18,181 --> 00:13:22,381
Please remember that managing stress is more important than medication.

212
00:13:25,421 --> 00:13:26,921
All right, we'll see you at your next appointment.

213
00:13:27,091 --> 00:13:28,191
Take care.

214
00:13:28,261 --> 00:13:30,991
(Hyujung Mental Health Clinic)

215
00:13:37,331 --> 00:13:38,830
(Did you get home safe? Are you at the venue?)

216
00:13:38,831 --> 00:13:40,331
(Call when you're free.)

217
00:13:46,811 --> 00:13:47,981
Surprise.

218
00:13:52,751 --> 00:13:54,681
What's with that reaction?

219
00:13:58,391 --> 00:13:59,391
What?

220
00:14:00,221 --> 00:14:01,221
Is something wrong?

221
00:14:01,721 --> 00:14:02,921
You scared the crap out of me, punk.

222
00:14:03,091 --> 00:14:04,291
You scared me half to death, you bastard.

223
00:14:04,391 --> 00:14:05,431
Hey!

224
00:14:05,691 --> 00:14:06,691
Come here.

225
00:14:08,601 --> 00:14:10,831
- Come here.
- Seriously?

226
00:14:13,101 --> 00:14:14,741
Ignoring my texts? You just blew me off.

227
00:14:15,401 --> 00:14:17,071
How dare you leave your brother on read?

228
00:14:18,371 --> 00:14:19,471
Goodbye, everyone.

229
00:14:19,811 --> 00:14:21,711
- Open the door, you jerk.
- All right!

230
00:14:21,981 --> 00:14:23,581
Hey, after running off like that the other night,

231
00:14:23,641 --> 00:14:25,911
you should've at least texted me to let me know you got home safe.

232
00:14:26,211 --> 00:14:27,251
That's rich.

233
00:14:27,511 --> 00:14:30,351
- Since when do I report to you?
- Get over here. Come here.

234
00:14:31,021 --> 00:14:32,051
Not again, cut it out.

235
00:14:40,931 --> 00:14:42,401
I couldn't sleep a wink that night.

236
00:14:44,701 --> 00:14:46,531
I called you out trying to cheer you up,

237
00:14:48,041 --> 00:14:49,741
and I was worried I just made you feel worse.

238
00:14:53,441 --> 00:14:54,681
You selfish brat.

239
00:14:59,381 --> 00:15:00,411
Whatever.

240
00:15:01,281 --> 00:15:04,051
Is it anything new that Dad chewed me out?

241
00:15:05,221 --> 00:15:07,291
Besides, everything he said was true anyway.

242
00:15:12,531 --> 00:15:13,531
Hyun Gu.

243
00:15:14,231 --> 00:15:15,561
I'm quitting comedy.

244
00:15:17,331 --> 00:15:18,331
What?

245
00:15:19,301 --> 00:15:20,671
We announced our disbandment yesterday,

246
00:15:21,441 --> 00:15:22,941
and now I'm going to wrap things up for good.

247
00:15:30,741 --> 00:15:33,081
- Because of Dad?
- No.

248
00:15:35,981 --> 00:15:37,951
- Because of me?
- What are you talking about?

249
00:15:38,021 --> 00:15:41,191
- Then why? Why are you doing this?
- There's no money in it.

250
00:15:41,991 --> 00:15:44,691
I'm sick of starving while pretending I'm winning at life.

251
00:15:45,031 --> 00:15:46,831
And it's not even fun anymore like it used to be.

252
00:15:47,461 --> 00:15:48,901
I just want to quit and make some real money.

253
00:15:50,961 --> 00:15:52,231
I'm going to get rich.

254
00:15:53,101 --> 00:15:54,101
Unbelievable...

255
00:15:56,841 --> 00:15:58,371
You tell Dad for me.

256
00:15:59,341 --> 00:16:00,971
Seeing how happy he would be...

257
00:16:01,911 --> 00:16:03,481
would make me sick to my stomach,

258
00:16:04,441 --> 00:16:06,111
so I really can't tell him myself.

259
00:16:19,991 --> 00:16:21,761
- Dad.
- Hey.

260
00:16:21,801 --> 00:16:24,031
- I'm back.
- Back already?

261
00:16:24,871 --> 00:16:27,270
I was going to pick you up as soon as I finished this.

262
00:16:27,271 --> 00:16:28,741
The appointment finished early.

263
00:16:29,301 --> 00:16:30,641
Tae Gu came to pick me up.

264
00:16:32,011 --> 00:16:34,611
Oh, really? That's a surprise.

265
00:16:35,781 --> 00:16:36,881
You must be tired.

266
00:16:38,851 --> 00:16:39,951
Let's go in and eat.

267
00:16:40,611 --> 00:16:41,651
Dad.

268
00:16:45,821 --> 00:16:47,451
Tae Gu says he's quitting comedy.

269
00:16:49,991 --> 00:16:53,561
He gave me all kinds of reasons, but it just sounded like nonsense.

270
00:16:56,101 --> 00:16:57,431
Something must have happened.

271
00:16:59,001 --> 00:17:00,201
Unbelievable.

272
00:17:01,341 --> 00:17:03,401
After digging his heels in all this time...

273
00:17:05,141 --> 00:17:06,211
Good for him.

274
00:17:06,941 --> 00:17:08,611
What a huge relief.

275
00:17:11,451 --> 00:17:12,511
Do you mean that?

276
00:17:15,021 --> 00:17:16,781
Is it really just a relief to you?

277
00:17:21,391 --> 00:17:23,221
Tae Gu takes after you so much.

278
00:17:26,491 --> 00:17:28,931
Finish packing up and come inside. I'll get dinner ready.

279
00:17:44,651 --> 00:17:45,811
Let's try it.

280
00:17:50,851 --> 00:17:52,491
Aren't you going to tell your family...

281
00:17:52,621 --> 00:17:53,851
that you're quitting comedy?

282
00:17:55,191 --> 00:17:56,421
My whole family is right here.

283
00:17:56,961 --> 00:17:59,461
The guys and you, boss.

284
00:18:04,201 --> 00:18:05,471
(Landlord)

285
00:18:06,101 --> 00:18:07,771
Boss, let me take this call real quick.

286
00:18:07,831 --> 00:18:09,771
- Work on this for a bit.
- Okay.

287
00:18:14,341 --> 00:18:15,641
It's such a shame, isn't it?

288
00:18:17,011 --> 00:18:20,711
He dropped out of medical school and cut ties with his family.

289
00:18:22,481 --> 00:18:24,051
Look at him now.

290
00:18:24,621 --> 00:18:27,651
They say a single choice can determine your whole life.

291
00:18:30,621 --> 00:18:32,661
Why are you skewering the green onion first?

292
00:18:33,361 --> 00:18:34,361
It doesn't matter.

293
00:18:34,431 --> 00:18:35,761
What do you mean it doesn't matter?

294
00:18:35,831 --> 00:18:38,101
One quick decision ruins the whole flavor.

295
00:18:38,171 --> 00:18:40,871
A skewer has to start with meat and end with meat.

296
00:18:43,701 --> 00:18:45,371
You always pick on me, seriously.

297
00:18:45,811 --> 00:18:47,911
Hello, ma'am. I sent yesterday's rent.

298
00:18:47,981 --> 00:18:49,811
I saw that,

299
00:18:50,241 --> 00:18:52,151
but you know the lease is up soon, right?

300
00:18:52,211 --> 00:18:53,411
What do you want to do?

301
00:18:57,321 --> 00:18:59,650
- We want to renew it, of course.
- Then you know you'll have to...

302
00:18:59,651 --> 00:19:01,661
pay a bit more rent this time, right?

303
00:19:02,221 --> 00:19:03,491
How much?

304
00:19:06,331 --> 00:19:07,331
Yes.

305
00:19:08,231 --> 00:19:11,131
Understood, yes. I'll talk it over with the guys.

306
00:19:13,631 --> 00:19:14,741
We're here.

307
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:17,341
- Hey.
- Welcome.

308
00:19:17,971 --> 00:19:19,911
Didn't you just eat with Na Yeon?

309
00:19:20,571 --> 00:19:23,011
I did, but I'm suddenly starving again.

310
00:19:27,481 --> 00:19:28,481
All right, look.

311
00:19:30,181 --> 00:19:31,181
What's that?

312
00:19:31,551 --> 00:19:32,991
Our list of things to wrap up.

313
00:19:34,021 --> 00:19:36,661
- Wrap up what?
- The payouts from our last shows,

314
00:19:36,721 --> 00:19:38,191
the car, and the place. We have to clear it all out.

315
00:19:39,061 --> 00:19:40,061
What?

316
00:19:40,691 --> 00:19:42,031
Why are you surprised?

317
00:19:42,231 --> 00:19:44,561
We bought the car for out-of-town gigs,

318
00:19:44,771 --> 00:19:46,331
so selling it makes sense. And the place...

319
00:19:46,401 --> 00:19:47,671
Wait, but about the place...

320
00:19:47,731 --> 00:19:50,001
Just because we're disbanding doesn't mean we have to split up.

321
00:19:51,441 --> 00:19:52,941
We don't have to live together either.

322
00:19:53,171 --> 00:19:56,581
We don't know where we'll get jobs, so why stay crammed together...

323
00:19:56,711 --> 00:19:57,911
near this expensive broadcasting station?

324
00:19:58,951 --> 00:20:02,351
We'll need money to start fresh. Better clear everything out...

325
00:20:02,421 --> 00:20:04,081
and split whatever cash we can get.

326
00:20:04,721 --> 00:20:05,721
Hey.

327
00:20:05,851 --> 00:20:08,091
How much was our security deposit again?

328
00:20:09,921 --> 00:20:13,031
- It's 20,000 dollars.
- 20,000 dollars...

329
00:20:13,191 --> 00:20:16,201
The lease ends around the same time as our final show,

330
00:20:17,131 --> 00:20:18,501
so we can get it back then.

331
00:20:19,271 --> 00:20:20,271
Okay.

332
00:20:20,801 --> 00:20:21,901
"Okay"?

333
00:20:22,371 --> 00:20:23,901
You're starting to hurt my feelings.

334
00:20:24,341 --> 00:20:25,341
Come on.

335
00:20:25,471 --> 00:20:27,671
Did you plan on living with me forever?

336
00:20:28,111 --> 00:20:29,141
Well, no...

337
00:20:30,981 --> 00:20:31,981
Oh, right.

338
00:20:32,051 --> 00:20:33,381
Didn't you have something to discuss?

339
00:20:35,721 --> 00:20:36,851
It's nothing.

340
00:20:39,121 --> 00:20:41,821
Over here. Come on in, hurry.

341
00:20:41,891 --> 00:20:43,421
Run, run, run!

342
00:20:47,591 --> 00:20:48,831
What's up?

343
00:20:50,461 --> 00:20:52,031
Hey, guys!

344
00:20:53,601 --> 00:20:55,271
Welcome to Korea.

345
00:20:56,971 --> 00:20:58,341
Where should we sit?

346
00:20:59,271 --> 00:21:02,641
You guys are here too? Sir, do you have tables for 20?

347
00:21:02,941 --> 00:21:05,050
Yes. Okay.

348
00:21:05,051 --> 00:21:07,251
Okay! All right. Let's go.

349
00:21:10,651 --> 00:21:15,361
One, two, three! Spread your wings wide!

350
00:21:15,621 --> 00:21:19,091
Fly freely through the sky!

351
00:21:19,161 --> 00:21:22,661
Singing and dancing

352
00:21:22,731 --> 00:21:26,201
I'm a beautiful butterfly!

353
00:21:26,801 --> 00:21:29,301
Man, it's not even Halloween. What's with this vibe?

354
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:30,971
I can't deal with this right now.

355
00:21:31,301 --> 00:21:33,571
What's this, Los Angeles or something?

356
00:21:34,041 --> 00:21:35,441
We can hang out here for a bit, right?

357
00:21:35,511 --> 00:21:37,841
Excuse me, miss. Could you please explain...

358
00:21:37,911 --> 00:21:39,681
what's going on here?

359
00:21:40,051 --> 00:21:43,451
Plans overlapped, so I just brought everyone together.

360
00:21:43,551 --> 00:21:45,791
It's more fun with a crowd.

361
00:21:46,491 --> 00:21:49,061
I'm an introvert. This is draining my energy.

362
00:21:49,691 --> 00:21:53,431
- Man Sik is a great singer.
- Sounds like a dying pig.

363
00:21:54,491 --> 00:21:57,631
Dodging the spiderwebs, I fly...

364
00:21:58,431 --> 00:22:00,971
Sorry about yesterday.

365
00:22:01,331 --> 00:22:04,741
- My sister was really in shock.
- No, no, it's fine.

366
00:22:04,801 --> 00:22:08,741
I don't know about him, but I took it as a good experience.

367
00:22:08,811 --> 00:22:10,711
When else would I go through something like that?

368
00:22:10,781 --> 00:22:13,211
- I looked at the bright side.
- An experience?

369
00:22:15,481 --> 00:22:18,391
You don't think this is all over, do you?

370
00:22:22,191 --> 00:22:24,861
Oh, you poor guys. What are we going to do?

371
00:22:26,991 --> 00:22:30,261
Listen carefully, guys.

372
00:22:31,261 --> 00:22:33,871
I bet I look crazy to you, right?

373
00:22:34,871 --> 00:22:37,701
Well, the real deal is my sister.

374
00:22:38,311 --> 00:22:40,541
If I'm just acting, she's the real deal.

375
00:22:40,611 --> 00:22:42,681
A bona fide lunatic.

376
00:22:45,081 --> 00:22:48,251
- She doesn't seem like that type.
- She seems normal usually.

377
00:22:48,321 --> 00:22:50,680
Gentle, cute.

378
00:22:50,681 --> 00:22:54,251
But once she snaps,

379
00:22:54,351 --> 00:22:56,291
she sees things through to the bitter end.

380
00:22:57,161 --> 00:22:59,191
She has this look in her eyes.

381
00:23:04,931 --> 00:23:07,331
That subtly unhinged look focused on its target.

382
00:23:07,631 --> 00:23:11,041
So innocent, yet so chilling.

383
00:23:30,691 --> 00:23:32,431
That was when I knew for sure.

384
00:23:32,791 --> 00:23:35,801
My sister isn't normal.

385
00:23:45,741 --> 00:23:48,281
Eun Young! What's this?

386
00:23:48,341 --> 00:23:49,481
Eun Young!

387
00:23:56,751 --> 00:23:57,921
I got it...

388
00:23:59,591 --> 00:24:00,591
What?

389
00:24:04,461 --> 00:24:08,931
Once she gets that look? It only ends when someone bleeds.

390
00:24:09,231 --> 00:24:10,361
Hey.

391
00:24:13,431 --> 00:24:15,971
Can you lend me some cash? Just five dollars.

392
00:24:16,041 --> 00:24:17,101
I'll pay you right back tomorrow.

393
00:24:19,571 --> 00:24:22,481
Yes! Hey, gather the others. Let's go.

394
00:24:23,481 --> 00:24:24,481
Nice one.

395
00:24:26,851 --> 00:24:27,851
My five dollars.

396
00:24:28,181 --> 00:24:30,421
I forgot. I'll give it to you later.

397
00:24:32,351 --> 00:24:33,351
When later?

398
00:24:33,851 --> 00:24:35,721
I said I'll give it to you.

399
00:24:36,061 --> 00:24:38,161
Stop annoying me over five lousy dollars.

400
00:24:42,331 --> 00:24:43,331
Darn it.

401
00:24:44,831 --> 00:24:45,831
Five dollars.

402
00:24:47,901 --> 00:24:48,971
How much is it?

403
00:24:52,611 --> 00:24:55,941
- Five dollars.
- Just give it to her.

404
00:24:56,011 --> 00:24:58,211
- Give it to her already.
- Five dollars.

405
00:24:58,481 --> 00:25:01,821
Seriously. She has a death wish.

406
00:25:04,451 --> 00:25:07,721
Or until they're bled completely dry.

407
00:25:09,161 --> 00:25:10,761
Oh, come on.

408
00:25:10,921 --> 00:25:13,731
- You're exaggerating a bit.
- I'm serious.

409
00:25:13,791 --> 00:25:15,501
Even with me running my mouth like this,

410
00:25:15,561 --> 00:25:17,560
I've never been beaten up once.

411
00:25:17,561 --> 00:25:20,431
Even the school bullies shivered at the mention of my sister's name.

412
00:25:21,001 --> 00:25:22,041
If you mess with her,

413
00:25:23,601 --> 00:25:24,701
you're screwed.

414
00:25:25,541 --> 00:25:26,541
And...

415
00:25:27,371 --> 00:25:28,711
yesterday,

416
00:25:29,641 --> 00:25:32,981
I saw that look again.

417
00:25:34,711 --> 00:25:35,721
Have a good day.

418
00:25:37,451 --> 00:25:39,091
So...

419
00:25:39,621 --> 00:25:41,451
are you telling us to be careful?

420
00:25:41,651 --> 00:25:43,961
I mean, thanks for the concern,

421
00:25:44,361 --> 00:25:46,461
but we're not exactly pushovers either.

422
00:25:47,231 --> 00:25:48,231
Especially...

423
00:25:48,731 --> 00:25:51,301
this guy. He isn't your average nutjob.

424
00:25:51,931 --> 00:25:52,931
Darn it.

425
00:25:59,471 --> 00:26:00,471
Hold on.

426
00:26:01,711 --> 00:26:02,981
Drinks are on me today.

427
00:26:36,011 --> 00:26:41,251
(Daeim International Co., Ltd. Go Eun Young)

428
00:26:59,771 --> 00:27:00,771
Who is it?

429
00:27:04,471 --> 00:27:06,011
- Good morning.
- Goodness.

430
00:27:07,071 --> 00:27:09,741
I made sure to check the expiration date this time.

431
00:27:11,141 --> 00:27:13,451
You're not disbanding, right?

432
00:27:15,281 --> 00:27:17,521
That subtly unhinged look focused on its target.

433
00:27:17,581 --> 00:27:20,821
So innocent, yet so chilling.

434
00:27:30,901 --> 00:27:32,631
(Asura)

435
00:27:34,131 --> 00:27:35,841
(Against)

436
00:27:38,611 --> 00:27:40,341
(Disbandment)

437
00:27:42,081 --> 00:27:43,411
It's on the house.

438
00:27:48,951 --> 00:27:50,481
Hey, Tae Gu. Hey...

439
00:27:50,981 --> 00:27:53,421
Hey, that's hot. Hey, doesn't that burn?

440
00:27:58,961 --> 00:28:00,091
You ruthless bastard.

441
00:28:01,091 --> 00:28:03,361
Would you like another cup?

442
00:28:06,531 --> 00:28:07,531
Guys.

443
00:28:09,471 --> 00:28:10,471
We're sold out.

444
00:28:10,971 --> 00:28:12,011
What?

445
00:28:12,141 --> 00:28:13,211
We sold out.

446
00:28:15,341 --> 00:28:17,341
- Sold out?
- Yes, completely.

447
00:28:23,721 --> 00:28:25,951
- Is this free?
- Yes.

448
00:28:27,151 --> 00:28:29,791
Please leave a review after watching the show.

449
00:28:30,121 --> 00:28:32,091
- Okay.
- Thank you.

450
00:28:49,581 --> 00:28:52,581
(Asura's Tenth Anniversary Special Show)

451
00:29:06,891 --> 00:29:09,431
(Comedy Town)

452
00:29:09,501 --> 00:29:12,271
(Asura's Tenth Anniversary Show)

453
00:29:18,771 --> 00:29:21,441
I waited so I could apologize.

454
00:29:21,981 --> 00:29:25,081
I just wanted to cheer you up.

455
00:29:26,911 --> 00:29:28,311
If I upset you,

456
00:29:29,681 --> 00:29:30,681
I'm truly...

457
00:29:31,821 --> 00:29:34,791
- sorry.
- You don't need to apologize.

458
00:29:34,851 --> 00:29:35,861
It's okay.

459
00:29:47,501 --> 00:29:48,501
Sure, well...

460
00:29:50,141 --> 00:29:52,011
- I get where you're coming from...
- But still.

461
00:29:54,271 --> 00:29:57,311
Could you please reconsider disbanding?

462
00:29:58,111 --> 00:30:00,611
I really hope you don't break up.

463
00:30:01,251 --> 00:30:02,251
Just once.

464
00:30:03,651 --> 00:30:06,251
Could you think it over one more time?

465
00:30:07,791 --> 00:30:08,791
Please?

466
00:30:11,491 --> 00:30:12,491
Hey, let's go.

467
00:30:15,191 --> 00:30:17,261
Hey, it's raining. Let's give her a ride.

468
00:30:17,561 --> 00:30:18,561
Hurry up.

469
00:30:19,601 --> 00:30:20,601
I'm sorry.

470
00:30:21,831 --> 00:30:22,841
Get home safe.

471
00:30:25,301 --> 00:30:26,811
- Take care.
- Cold-hearted jerk.

472
00:30:54,601 --> 00:30:56,171
Didn't you take it a bit too far?

473
00:30:56,701 --> 00:30:57,701
What?

474
00:30:58,201 --> 00:31:00,611
Seriously, leaving a woman all by herself...

475
00:31:01,311 --> 00:31:03,211
in the middle of the night in the rain?

476
00:31:03,281 --> 00:31:05,081
I left her alone precisely because she's a woman.

477
00:31:05,581 --> 00:31:07,811
If she were a guy, I would've beaten the crap out of him.

478
00:31:08,511 --> 00:31:10,151
Did you really have to put it that way?

479
00:31:11,181 --> 00:31:12,191
What?

480
00:31:13,091 --> 00:31:14,391
I'm actually grateful to her.

481
00:31:16,091 --> 00:31:18,021
She's doing this because she loves our trio.

482
00:31:19,231 --> 00:31:20,991
Grateful, my foot. She's so annoying.

483
00:31:21,991 --> 00:31:23,561
Whatever. It's pissing me off, so drop it.

484
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:27,231
You ruthless bastard. You make me sick, seriously.

485
00:31:31,371 --> 00:31:34,141
Hey, want me to cheer you guys up?

486
00:31:34,711 --> 00:31:37,381
- Guess who I met yesterday.
- I couldn't care less.

487
00:31:39,651 --> 00:31:40,811
I went to see CEO Shin.

488
00:31:41,711 --> 00:31:43,681
We're getting all that gig money he stiffed us on.

489
00:31:45,181 --> 00:31:47,091
For real? That scumbag agreed to pay?

490
00:31:47,251 --> 00:31:48,251
Yes.

491
00:31:48,621 --> 00:31:50,791
I threatened to report him, and he rolled right over.

492
00:31:51,491 --> 00:31:52,631
It comes to about 4,000 dollars.

493
00:31:52,861 --> 00:31:55,361
Once we get the apartment deposit and sort everything else out,

494
00:31:55,601 --> 00:31:57,331
I think we can walk away with about 10,000 dollars each.

495
00:31:57,401 --> 00:32:00,331
Gosh. Man, that's insane.

496
00:32:00,401 --> 00:32:02,101
I thought we'd never see that money.

497
00:32:02,171 --> 00:32:03,401
- Right?
- Right?

498
00:32:17,451 --> 00:32:18,451
Nice.

499
00:32:18,951 --> 00:32:20,391
The person you're calling is unavailable...

500
00:32:21,191 --> 00:32:23,321
Where on earth did she go?

501
00:32:48,381 --> 00:32:50,081
You're back?

502
00:32:52,421 --> 00:32:55,521
Eun Young! What happened to you?

503
00:33:00,791 --> 00:33:02,501
I'm so furious, seriously.

504
00:33:02,901 --> 00:33:05,631
How could they leave someone behind in this pouring rain?

505
00:33:07,301 --> 00:33:10,001
That's not what happened, I...

506
00:33:10,071 --> 00:33:11,641
Forget it. Stop taking their side. It's annoying.

507
00:33:12,471 --> 00:33:14,211
It's really not like that.

508
00:33:17,911 --> 00:33:18,911
Eun Young.

509
00:33:19,951 --> 00:33:21,181
Just stop it now.

510
00:33:21,311 --> 00:33:22,421
Even I'd hate it.

511
00:33:22,481 --> 00:33:24,581
Stopping someone who wants to quit...

512
00:33:25,851 --> 00:33:27,191
That's not cheering them on.

513
00:33:27,821 --> 00:33:28,921
That's just harassing them.

514
00:33:30,961 --> 00:33:32,791
(Asura)

515
00:33:36,531 --> 00:33:39,101
I know. I do.

516
00:33:39,831 --> 00:33:41,571
Then why are you doing this?

517
00:33:45,841 --> 00:33:46,911
Ji Young.

518
00:33:48,271 --> 00:33:49,281
I'm...

519
00:33:55,511 --> 00:33:56,521
I'm...

520
00:34:00,751 --> 00:34:01,991
I'm so cold.

521
00:34:06,931 --> 00:34:08,591
Dry your hair.

522
00:34:09,531 --> 00:34:11,501
(Soojung Villa)

523
00:34:11,561 --> 00:34:13,531
(No Unauthorized Parking)

524
00:34:19,411 --> 00:34:21,341
(Deposit: 4,000 Dollars Hwanggu Media Co., Ltd.)

525
00:34:27,311 --> 00:34:28,311
Hello.

526
00:34:32,821 --> 00:34:34,891
Looks like you're heading to your part-time job.

527
00:34:35,291 --> 00:34:37,421
- Yes.
- Did you get home safely yesterday?

528
00:34:37,791 --> 00:34:39,631
- Yes.
- My sister is sick.

529
00:34:39,691 --> 00:34:41,161
She got completely soaked in the rain,

530
00:34:41,231 --> 00:34:42,561
caught a summer cold, of all things,

531
00:34:42,631 --> 00:34:43,831
and now she's hovering between life and death.

532
00:34:43,901 --> 00:34:45,461
So I'm out getting medicine.

533
00:34:46,931 --> 00:34:48,831
Liquid medicine usually works better than pills.

534
00:34:49,641 --> 00:34:50,741
Get that next time.

535
00:35:03,251 --> 00:35:04,251
Hyun Kyung.

536
00:35:05,921 --> 00:35:07,651
Why do I even care?

537
00:35:16,531 --> 00:35:17,961
I'm stepping out for a bit.

538
00:35:18,131 --> 00:35:19,471
Eat your porridge and take your medicine.

539
00:35:56,301 --> 00:35:57,301
Which unit is it?

540
00:36:17,491 --> 00:36:18,521
I like you.

541
00:36:23,801 --> 00:36:25,001
What?

542
00:36:30,971 --> 00:36:32,541
What are you talking about?

543
00:36:39,611 --> 00:36:43,181
You asked me on the rooftop before. About having something I love.

544
00:36:44,281 --> 00:36:45,921
Something everyone says is wrong,

545
00:36:47,251 --> 00:36:48,851
but I can't live without.

546
00:36:48,921 --> 00:36:50,161
You asked if I had anything like that.

547
00:36:52,661 --> 00:36:55,531
For me, that's Asura.

548
00:36:57,301 --> 00:36:58,561
It's all of you.

549
00:37:02,371 --> 00:37:05,341
- Unbelievable.
- So, I'm sorry, but...

550
00:37:07,571 --> 00:37:09,211
I'm not going to give up.

551
00:37:09,881 --> 00:37:11,281
Once I get better,

552
00:37:12,041 --> 00:37:13,451
I'm going to follow you around again.

553
00:37:14,751 --> 00:37:16,621
I'll keep following you relentlessly,

554
00:37:17,581 --> 00:37:18,881
bothering you,

555
00:37:19,821 --> 00:37:21,121
and driving you crazy.

556
00:37:23,591 --> 00:37:24,861
You're a lunatic...

557
00:37:28,631 --> 00:37:31,130
- You're out of your mind.
- Are you angry?

558
00:37:31,131 --> 00:37:32,931
Do I look like I'm having fun right now?

559
00:37:38,941 --> 00:37:39,971
But you know,

560
00:37:42,011 --> 00:37:43,341
strangely,

561
00:37:44,781 --> 00:37:45,981
in my eyes,

562
00:37:48,651 --> 00:37:50,151
you keep looking sad.

563
00:37:51,981 --> 00:37:54,891
You don't look angry. You look sad.

564
00:37:58,321 --> 00:37:59,391
Am I wrong?

565
00:38:14,671 --> 00:38:17,041
I can't believe this.

566
00:38:18,481 --> 00:38:19,751
You really are sick.

567
00:38:21,411 --> 00:38:23,021
You're seriously sick right now.

568
00:38:24,651 --> 00:38:26,991
You must think I'm a pushover just because I hear you out,

569
00:38:28,121 --> 00:38:30,121
so stay 100 meters away from me.

570
00:38:30,661 --> 00:38:31,961
Don't talk to me,

571
00:38:33,391 --> 00:38:34,531
and don't even come near me.

572
00:38:35,391 --> 00:38:36,601
Otherwise, I really will...

573
00:38:38,901 --> 00:38:40,231
report you to the police.

574
00:38:55,181 --> 00:38:58,251
Comedy trio, Asura.

575
00:39:00,891 --> 00:39:01,891
You're back.

576
00:39:10,201 --> 00:39:13,131
What's wrong? What is it? Hey.

577
00:39:14,471 --> 00:39:15,501
What are you doing?

578
00:39:17,371 --> 00:39:20,941
Hey. Wait, hey, what are you doing?

579
00:39:21,411 --> 00:39:22,411
Hey!

580
00:39:27,551 --> 00:39:29,481
You said you would call. Why haven't you?

581
00:39:29,681 --> 00:39:32,251
If you don't answer by the weekend, I'll assume you're not renewing.

582
00:39:40,191 --> 00:39:41,691
(Glass Bottles, Cans, Scrap Metal)

583
00:39:54,371 --> 00:39:57,041
Darn it. Why is he doing that?

584
00:39:58,011 --> 00:40:00,651
Hey, that will break. Be careful. Seriously.

585
00:40:02,881 --> 00:40:03,881
Jun Seo.

586
00:40:04,851 --> 00:40:06,591
Stop him. I think he's lost his mind.

587
00:40:10,591 --> 00:40:11,591
What's he doing?

588
00:40:11,661 --> 00:40:14,060
I don't know. He came back acting like this.

589
00:40:14,061 --> 00:40:15,161
He says he's clearing things out.

590
00:40:15,231 --> 00:40:16,831
Now that we've decided, we should get it over with.

591
00:40:17,201 --> 00:40:18,931
Trash what we can trash, sell what we can sell.

592
00:40:19,371 --> 00:40:20,431
How much should I list this for?

593
00:40:20,771 --> 00:40:21,801
You're throwing that away too?

594
00:40:22,101 --> 00:40:25,371
- Hey, this is our debut outfit.
- What does that matter now?

595
00:40:25,441 --> 00:40:26,441
It's over anyway.

596
00:40:26,641 --> 00:40:29,111
- It's just garbage now.
- Seriously, man.

597
00:40:29,211 --> 00:40:31,111
Are you money-crazy? Just sell your own stuff, darn it.

598
00:40:34,151 --> 00:40:35,681
What's the big rush?

599
00:40:38,481 --> 00:40:39,491
Hey.

600
00:40:40,691 --> 00:40:41,691
Hey.

601
00:40:43,591 --> 00:40:44,591
Hey.

602
00:40:45,691 --> 00:40:47,461
What's the big rush?

603
00:40:59,341 --> 00:41:01,441
As soon as we decided to disband, you canceled the show,

604
00:41:01,611 --> 00:41:03,341
and you went ahead and announced it right away.

605
00:41:04,281 --> 00:41:05,381
I put up with it back then.

606
00:41:06,051 --> 00:41:08,051
First the car, then the place, and now...

607
00:41:08,411 --> 00:41:09,681
you're even doing this.

608
00:41:10,681 --> 00:41:11,681
Hey.

609
00:41:12,081 --> 00:41:14,091
It's like you were just waiting for us to disband.

610
00:41:14,691 --> 00:41:15,691
Do you realize that?

611
00:41:18,761 --> 00:41:20,461
It's been ten years. Ten years.

612
00:41:22,261 --> 00:41:25,161
All these things that you're getting rid of in a hurry...

613
00:41:25,301 --> 00:41:28,971
are things we cherished and built together over ten whole years.

614
00:41:30,141 --> 00:41:31,501
How is this so easy for you?

615
00:41:32,371 --> 00:41:33,811
How can it be this easy?

616
00:41:35,011 --> 00:41:36,981
Hey, okay. Hold on.

617
00:41:37,281 --> 00:41:39,781
You both seem pretty worked up, so let's sit down and talk.

618
00:41:40,681 --> 00:41:41,881
Let me ask you one thing.

619
00:41:43,321 --> 00:41:44,681
Does this really not bother you at all?

620
00:41:47,291 --> 00:41:48,491
You have zero regrets?

621
00:41:53,961 --> 00:41:54,961
Yes.

622
00:41:56,431 --> 00:41:57,431
None.

623
00:42:02,841 --> 00:42:04,201
What's there to regret?

624
00:42:06,771 --> 00:42:08,040
Shows where we scream our lungs out promoting...

625
00:42:08,041 --> 00:42:09,741
just to get barely ten people to show up?

626
00:42:11,341 --> 00:42:12,881
This tiny two-room dump?

627
00:42:14,351 --> 00:42:16,551
That piece-of-crap car that breaks down every other day?

628
00:42:17,421 --> 00:42:18,521
What, exactly?

629
00:42:20,451 --> 00:42:21,521
Jun Seo.

630
00:42:23,421 --> 00:42:24,961
We failed.

631
00:42:26,461 --> 00:42:27,991
Look at us.

632
00:42:28,791 --> 00:42:31,961
Stuck in a shoebox, not a penny to our names,

633
00:42:32,031 --> 00:42:33,771
just three grown men getting older...

634
00:42:36,671 --> 00:42:37,901
We're failures.

635
00:42:38,971 --> 00:42:40,211
Total, complete failures.

636
00:42:42,141 --> 00:42:43,181
And you have regrets?

637
00:42:44,981 --> 00:42:47,351
Do you, really? Seriously?

638
00:42:51,321 --> 00:42:53,491
Once we decided to disband, it all hit me.

639
00:42:57,061 --> 00:42:59,691
No wonder people laughed at us the way they did.

640
00:43:02,431 --> 00:43:03,901
We were truly pathetic.

641
00:43:08,231 --> 00:43:10,001
- What?
- So I just want to wrap this up...

642
00:43:12,271 --> 00:43:13,471
as fast as possible...

643
00:43:15,641 --> 00:43:16,881
and start a new life, okay?

644
00:43:19,241 --> 00:43:20,451
So please, just cooperate.

645
00:43:26,521 --> 00:43:27,851
And cut it out with the regret nonsense.

646
00:43:30,291 --> 00:43:31,291
All right?

647
00:43:36,161 --> 00:43:38,301
Hey, Kang Tae Gu. Hey.

648
00:43:38,761 --> 00:43:42,101
Hey, stop, freeze right there. Hey, you jerk, hey.

649
00:43:42,271 --> 00:43:43,901
Hey, Kang Tae Gu. Tae Gu.

650
00:43:51,441 --> 00:43:52,441
Jun Seo.

651
00:43:52,581 --> 00:43:54,511
Just let it go for now. You know he has no middle ground.

652
00:44:00,521 --> 00:44:02,961
Darn it. What am I supposed to do?

653
00:44:08,691 --> 00:44:11,701
(Clothing Donation Bin)

654
00:44:14,601 --> 00:44:15,601
What's that?

655
00:44:16,841 --> 00:44:18,971
- Kimchi fried rice...
- Back off, will you?

656
00:44:19,171 --> 00:44:20,771
- Why?
- Go away.

657
00:44:21,871 --> 00:44:23,711
Jun Seo, you're leaving? I made food.

658
00:44:24,841 --> 00:44:26,711
Hey, eat before you go. It's all ready.

659
00:44:29,081 --> 00:44:30,121
See you later.

660
00:44:30,981 --> 00:44:33,451
Hey, have a good one. Watch out for cars!

661
00:44:35,951 --> 00:44:36,961
You jerk.

662
00:44:38,061 --> 00:44:39,221
Do you have any tact at all?

663
00:44:39,891 --> 00:44:41,361
Because of you, I'm stuck in the middle.

664
00:44:44,231 --> 00:44:45,361
You didn't make a fried egg?

665
00:44:45,661 --> 00:44:48,571
- Why you... Seriously.
- What's your problem?

666
00:44:53,141 --> 00:44:54,141
Hey.

667
00:44:54,971 --> 00:44:56,911
I know when your mind is made up,

668
00:44:57,581 --> 00:44:58,881
but consider how he feels.

669
00:44:59,881 --> 00:45:00,951
Is that really so hard?

670
00:45:01,351 --> 00:45:02,411
I'm only making one for myself.

671
00:45:02,921 --> 00:45:03,921
Just try touching it.

672
00:45:05,051 --> 00:45:06,521
I should just kill you.

673
00:45:19,231 --> 00:45:20,631
You were a social studies teacher?

674
00:45:21,071 --> 00:45:22,071
No way.

675
00:45:22,131 --> 00:45:23,701
I totally thought you were a musician.

676
00:45:23,771 --> 00:45:27,111
I mean, when you sang earlier, I almost completely fell for you.

677
00:45:28,041 --> 00:45:29,581
Oh, come on.

678
00:45:31,241 --> 00:45:32,281
Well, I mean,

679
00:45:32,341 --> 00:45:33,981
back in the day at the school festival,

680
00:45:34,051 --> 00:45:35,110
whenever I sang,

681
00:45:35,111 --> 00:45:37,181
the girls would threaten to report me.

682
00:45:37,751 --> 00:45:38,821
For marriage, that is.

683
00:45:43,691 --> 00:45:47,461
Nam Il. Come take a break over here. Just for a bit.

684
00:45:47,891 --> 00:45:50,831
- Gosh, it's hot.
- Hello.

685
00:45:50,931 --> 00:45:53,531
Look at my little freeloaders, here to sponge off me.

686
00:45:53,601 --> 00:45:55,871
- Oh, you're here too. Hi there.
- Hello.

687
00:45:56,441 --> 00:45:57,541
Honey.

688
00:45:58,141 --> 00:45:59,141
We're back.

689
00:46:00,211 --> 00:46:01,611
Sir, I'm going to take out the trash.

690
00:46:04,641 --> 00:46:06,911
Hey, what's his deal lately? Did you guys fight again?

691
00:46:07,051 --> 00:46:08,811
The guilty party is acting completely unfazed,

692
00:46:08,881 --> 00:46:11,181
and I'm the one stuck in the middle, dying inside.

693
00:46:11,851 --> 00:46:14,791
- Yes! It sold.
- What did you sell?

694
00:46:14,851 --> 00:46:16,421
I've got to go. They want it shipped right away.

695
00:46:16,491 --> 00:46:17,621
Boss, I'm taking off.

696
00:46:17,921 --> 00:46:20,891
Get out. Go on, you 99 percent gentleman. Get lost.

697
00:46:22,561 --> 00:46:23,801
I'm back.

698
00:46:25,331 --> 00:46:28,831
- You're back?
- Your face is still red.

699
00:46:29,171 --> 00:46:30,201
Did you take your medicine?

700
00:46:32,371 --> 00:46:34,511
- Where were you?
- The skewer place.

701
00:46:34,911 --> 00:46:36,611
I just watched some serious drama unfold.

702
00:46:37,811 --> 00:46:39,381
Jun Seo and Tae Gu got into a fight.

703
00:46:39,811 --> 00:46:42,011
They haven't spoken to each other for two days straight.

704
00:46:42,481 --> 00:46:44,321
- Why?
- What do you mean, why?

705
00:46:44,521 --> 00:46:46,080
Even if they agreed to quit, wrapping everything up...

706
00:46:46,081 --> 00:46:48,421
like he was waiting for it would tick anyone off.

707
00:46:48,791 --> 00:46:51,560
Earlier, Jun Seo made it so obvious...

708
00:46:51,561 --> 00:46:53,391
that he was deeply hurt, radiating it with his entire body,

709
00:46:53,531 --> 00:46:55,490
but Tae Gu didn't care at all.

710
00:46:55,491 --> 00:46:56,861
If anything, he seemed thrilled.

711
00:46:58,001 --> 00:47:00,571
He's so cold-hearted.

712
00:47:09,041 --> 00:47:11,781
(Soojung Villa)

713
00:47:28,391 --> 00:47:29,761
(Tasty Pizza)

714
00:47:30,131 --> 00:47:31,201
I'm back.

715
00:47:31,601 --> 00:47:32,801
Don't take your helmet off.

716
00:47:33,071 --> 00:47:34,271
You have to head right back out, okay?

717
00:47:34,331 --> 00:47:35,931
I only have five minutes left on my shift.

718
00:47:36,271 --> 00:47:37,271
- Where is it?
- It's nearby.

719
00:47:37,341 --> 00:47:38,471
Won't even take five minutes.

720
00:47:38,541 --> 00:47:41,571
(Delivery Address: Gag Jirak Green Room, QBN New Hall)

721
00:48:06,701 --> 00:48:08,531
Pizza delivery!

722
00:48:08,801 --> 00:48:11,001
Hey, guys, let's eat first.

723
00:48:11,371 --> 00:48:13,241
- Let's eat first.
- Good to see you again.

724
00:48:13,811 --> 00:48:14,811
Hey, Tae Gu.

725
00:48:15,641 --> 00:48:16,711
Hey, Tae Gu.

726
00:48:17,141 --> 00:48:19,341
Are you new here? Why would you order from there?

727
00:48:19,541 --> 00:48:21,911
- I'm sorry. I didn't know.
- Hey.

728
00:48:22,311 --> 00:48:23,351
Good call.

729
00:48:23,651 --> 00:48:25,381
Our place makes the best pizza around here.

730
00:48:26,421 --> 00:48:27,421
Fastest delivery, too.

731
00:48:29,861 --> 00:48:30,861
Tae Gu.

732
00:48:31,661 --> 00:48:33,161
Is it true you're quitting comedy?

733
00:48:33,631 --> 00:48:35,291
What? Yes, that's how it turned out.

734
00:48:37,231 --> 00:48:39,361
Here, I upgraded the sodas on the house.

735
00:48:40,031 --> 00:48:41,201
Who's taking care of the bill?

736
00:48:41,601 --> 00:48:42,871
Oh, I'll get it.

737
00:48:48,311 --> 00:48:50,041
I can't believe him...

738
00:48:58,781 --> 00:48:59,851
Here you go.

739
00:49:00,391 --> 00:49:01,621
All right, keep up the good work.

740
00:49:02,091 --> 00:49:04,221
- Take care, sir.
- Goodbye, sir.

741
00:49:04,291 --> 00:49:06,421
- Thank you.
- Sure, sit back down.

742
00:49:06,931 --> 00:49:07,931
Keep at it!

743
00:49:12,501 --> 00:49:15,501
(Gag Jirak)

744
00:50:27,071 --> 00:50:28,211
I'll give it a try.

745
00:50:29,071 --> 00:50:30,941
- I'll head down.
- Okay.

746
00:50:31,541 --> 00:50:32,541
Okay.

747
00:50:33,681 --> 00:50:35,611
- Come on, look quickly.
- Okay.

748
00:50:37,181 --> 00:50:38,751
All right, let's take it slow.

749
00:50:40,121 --> 00:50:41,421
A little more back, just a bit more.

750
00:50:41,491 --> 00:50:42,991
- Help him up. Check it.
- Okay.

751
00:50:45,491 --> 00:50:47,591
- Oh, yes?
- Did you check it?

752
00:51:10,381 --> 00:51:12,620
Hey, it's been a while since we drank just the two of us.

753
00:51:12,621 --> 00:51:13,690
Cheers.

754
00:51:13,691 --> 00:51:14,751
Here.

755
00:51:23,091 --> 00:51:24,531
What's taking Tae Gu so long?

756
00:52:11,881 --> 00:52:13,951
- What are you doing there?
- You're back?

757
00:52:23,251 --> 00:52:24,391
Because it felt like such a waste.

758
00:52:26,361 --> 00:52:27,991
Every single one of these holds meaning,

759
00:52:29,331 --> 00:52:33,231
and I thought you might regret it later.

760
00:52:36,131 --> 00:52:38,741
They said they would never sell that wig,

761
00:52:38,801 --> 00:52:39,871
so I couldn't get it back.

762
00:52:41,371 --> 00:52:42,371
And this...

763
00:52:44,341 --> 00:52:45,941
I washed it as best as I could,

764
00:52:46,711 --> 00:52:48,581
but it was already stained.

765
00:53:03,561 --> 00:53:04,561
What are you doing?

766
00:53:08,871 --> 00:53:10,501
Who do you think you are?

767
00:53:13,241 --> 00:53:15,441
Who are you to keep crossing the line?

768
00:53:17,841 --> 00:53:19,081
Isn't that Tae Gu's voice?

769
00:53:20,911 --> 00:53:22,281
I told you clearly, didn't I?

770
00:53:23,211 --> 00:53:24,421
That we can't turn back.

771
00:53:24,981 --> 00:53:26,451
That it's already decided.

772
00:53:27,391 --> 00:53:30,291
So why do you keep bothering me like this? Why?

773
00:53:36,131 --> 00:53:37,461
Why am I doing this?

774
00:53:41,401 --> 00:53:43,001
That's what I want to ask.

775
00:53:44,071 --> 00:53:46,041
Why are you doing this?

776
00:53:47,141 --> 00:53:48,471
Doing things you don't even mean,

777
00:53:48,541 --> 00:53:50,081
hurting others and getting hurt yourself.

778
00:53:51,081 --> 00:53:52,911
What on earth are you thinking?

779
00:53:55,251 --> 00:53:57,821
- Here we go again.
- Tell me...

780
00:53:58,381 --> 00:53:59,521
what you're thinking.

781
00:54:00,921 --> 00:54:02,851
- Why you're acting like this...
- Are you delusional?

782
00:54:05,021 --> 00:54:07,031
Get lost before I actually call the cops.

783
00:54:07,191 --> 00:54:09,091
- Tell me!
- If I do,

784
00:54:11,201 --> 00:54:12,631
would you even understand how I feel?

785
00:54:12,701 --> 00:54:15,101
Yes, I'll understand.

786
00:54:18,001 --> 00:54:19,171
So tell me.

787
00:54:24,511 --> 00:54:26,411
Something you couldn't give up for ten years,

788
00:54:27,111 --> 00:54:28,581
and you suddenly hate it in an instant?

789
00:54:28,911 --> 00:54:32,151
- You expect me to believe that?
- Yes. I hate it now.

790
00:54:33,321 --> 00:54:34,391
I hate it.

791
00:54:35,291 --> 00:54:36,921
It's terrible. I loathe it to death!

792
00:54:36,991 --> 00:54:38,361
How could you?

793
00:54:40,861 --> 00:54:41,991
You said you loved it.

794
00:54:44,831 --> 00:54:46,001
You said it was your dream.

795
00:54:54,441 --> 00:54:55,541
Because I felt sorry.

796
